WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.534
-Welcome back.

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.634
It is so great to see you.

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.367
Thank you so much
for being on the show.

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.133
-I have to acknowledge
Questlove, though.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:07.667
His -- That documentary,

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:09.767
"Summer Of Soul" was --
-Yep. That was --

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:11.400
-Congratulations.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.467
-Thank you.
-He nailed it.

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:16.100
Every time you're here,
we always have a good time.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.467
I want to talk to you
about everything.

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:19.033
But, first, I want to talk
to you about --

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.834
You're an unbelievable actor.

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:22.901
You're an unbelievable activist.

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:25.033
And then, you changed
the entire game with

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:26.767
"The Jane Fonda Workout."

00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:28.067
-Oh, yeah, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:31.133
That came out 40 --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:32.267
I was doing --
I was checking it out.

00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:33.667
It came out 40 years ago.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:36.868
Did you have any idea
that it was going to be as big?

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:39.567
-Oh, absolutely.
It was totally strategic.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:41.033
The timing of it.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:43.601
Not.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:45.067
I took a class with a woman --

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:47.234
a talented woman
name Leni Cazden,

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:49.501
and it became a blockbuster,

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:51.367
and I did not expect it,
the whole thing.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:54.868
You know, I got all these
musicians to give me songs,

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:57.133
because it came out
first as a record.

00:00:57.133 --> 00:00:59.534
And, of course, they all agreed
to it, because they didn't --

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:01.200
they didn't think
it was going to be anything.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.434
And they didn't even ask
for a percentage

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:04.734
or anything like that.

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:06.234
-Yeah, they just --
well, I have -- This is the --

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.033
This is the workout album.

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:09.734
This is the album right here.
Look at this.

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:12.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:12.801 --> 00:01:14.033
You have Jimmy Buffett on here.

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:15.200
You have REO Speedwagon.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.467
The Jacksons are on here.

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:18.868
This is a great album.

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:21.334
I think you invented
the very first gym playlist.

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:23.334
-For sure. Yeah. Who knew?

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.133
-Who knew this is it?
-Yes.

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:28.868
-What is the exercise
playlist you have today?

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:33.367
-Oh, honey, there's no song
slow enough for me

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:35.467
to do a workout to.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:38.267
-Is that right?
-It's all --

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:39.667
I'm almost 85 years old.

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:40.801
You can't move fast.

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:42.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wow.

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:43.767
Almost 85?

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:47.000
You look so good.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.968
-Yeah, you look pretty
good yourself too, I must say.

00:01:48.968 --> 00:01:50.133
-Thank you, pal.

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:51.133
-We were all talking
about it backstage.

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:54.200
-Look, I want to --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.834
You know, you're always
doing something new.

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:57.200
And last time we were here,
we were talking about

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.367
the live stream series you did,
"Fire Drill Fridays."

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:00.234
-Yeah, still doing it.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:01.334
Mm-hmm.
-Yeah.

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:02.467
It brings attention
to climate change.

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:04.033
But now you've taken it
a step further.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:05.267
Okay.

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.100
You've launched the Jane Fonda
Climate PAC.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.133
-That's right.

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:08.801
-Can you tell
everyone about this?

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:10.033
-Sure.

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:13.267
Well, you've got to have
the rallies and the --

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:16.033
and we're gonna do
in-person rallies again.

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:18.334
Tune in to "Fire Drill Fridays"
on Fridays,

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:20.868
and I'll tell you all about
what we're going to be doing

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:22.934
leading up
to the midterm elections.

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:25.367
But what I've learned,
what we've all learned,

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:27.734
is that it's not enough.

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:31.801
The fossil-fuel industry has a
stranglehold on our government.

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:34.701
They give money to Democrats
and to Republicans,

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:36.868
and we've got to get
rid of those types

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:39.267
that take money
from the fossil-fuel industry.

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:42.033
And we'll replace them
with climate champions

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:43.968
who really will work
for the people

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:45.801
and not for big corporations.

00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:48.300
That's what the Jane Fonda
Climate PAC does.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
And -- Yes.

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:56.367
Out.
-I think we all want this.

00:02:56.367 --> 00:03:00.234
-Next week I'm going to be
in Michigan for Andy Levin.

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:03.100
I'm going to be working for him,
for Barbara Lee,

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.534
for Donna Edwards.

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:07.400
I mean, there's some great
climate champions out there

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.400
that we need to support,
because tens of millions

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.567
of dollars are in
to trying to defeat them.

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:16.067
And so, if you want to join us
and find out more, thejanepac --

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:17.667
P-A-C --
dot com.

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:18.834
Janepac.com.
-Yeah, Janepac.

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:20.167
That's what I'm talking about
right there.

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:21.634
-That's it.
-I love that you're doing this.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:22.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:27.567
We all want --
We all want this.

00:03:27.567 --> 00:03:29.434
When you're not busy
saving the planet,

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:32.000
you're also still doing movies.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.367
I just saw this cast right here,

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:36.300
if I can just show
a picture of this.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.033
Some awesome VIPs here.

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.934
But one person sticks out
in my head a little bit.

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:43.534
This is Rita Moreno, this is
Lily Tomlin, Tom Brady --

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:44.868
-Sally Field.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:46.367
-Tom -- I said Tom Brady.

00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:47.634
Yeah.

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.501
That's -- I mean,
that's really Tom Brady?

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:51.467
-Oh, he's so cute.
-Yeah, he really is.

00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:53.367
[ Laughter ]
-And nice.

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:55.467
-He is so cute and nice.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:57.167
What is this?

00:03:57.167 --> 00:04:01.033
-It's a partly true story
about four women in their 80s --

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:04.334
Well, Rita is 90 and Sally
is 75, but who's counting?

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:06.434
-Who's counting? Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:09.467
Who have a real thing for Tom
Brady for all kinds of reasons.

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:11.200
And we have adventures.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:14.000
We go to the famous game
in Houston

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.400
where they were down --
way, way down --

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.834
and they came back.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:19.767
-That's the game --
-He's done some amazing things.

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:20.934
-Oh, my God.

00:04:20.934 --> 00:04:21.868
-He's kind of a magician,
that guy.

00:04:21.868 --> 00:04:22.834
Have you met Tom --
-Yeah.

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:25.334
And I had a scene
with Gronkowski.

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:28.300
See, my character writes
sex novels about football.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.300
So I wrote --
She wrote a book.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.067
She wrote a book --
[ Cheers ]

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:36.167
♪♪
-I like this.

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:37.567
-What? She wrote a book called

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:40.000
"Between a Gronk
and a Hard Place."

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:47.100
I had a funny little scene
with Gronk.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:48.767
And, oh, man, is he funny.

00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:50.133
-He's a great guy too.
-And is he tall.

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:51.968
-He's fun.
He's a blast.

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:54.634
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:56.834
I want you to come back, please,
when that film comes out.

00:04:56.834 --> 00:04:59.334
But we're here tonight
to talk about --

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:01.767
you play the dragon in "Luck."

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:04.934
-I do.
-This beautiful animated movie.

00:05:04.934 --> 00:05:06.434
-She's a great character.

00:05:06.434 --> 00:05:10.000
-I mean, that's fun to --
Do you like doing voice-overs?

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.767
-I've wanted to break in to
voice-overs in a feature film.

00:05:12.767 --> 00:05:14.734
This is my first feature film.

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:17.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:22.400
Partly because I love animated
films, partly because I'm old,

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.467
and it's a really good gig
for an old person.

00:05:24.467 --> 00:05:26.567
You don't have to worry about
how you look and your hair

00:05:26.567 --> 00:05:28.033
and all that kind of thing.

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:29.534
You know,
you just go and have fun.

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:30.968
And it was really fun.
-Yeah, show up in your pajamas.

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:32.434
And, yeah, you go --
-Yeah, you can go

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:33.734
in your pajamas.

00:05:33.734 --> 00:05:35.534
She's -- You know,
she's very flirtatious.

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:38.634
She's the CEO
of the kingdom of Luck.

00:05:38.634 --> 00:05:40.601
-Yeah, I love the story
about it all too.

00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:42.167
-It's a wonderful story.
-It is fun.

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:44.234
And they know how to do it
over there over at Apple TV+.

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:45.834
-Yeah, Skydance.

00:05:45.834 --> 00:05:47.133
-I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:05:47.133 --> 00:05:49.868
Here's Jane Fonda
as the dragon in "Luck."

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:51.033
Take a look at this.

00:05:51.033 --> 00:05:54.167
♪♪

00:05:54.167 --> 00:05:56.067
-Twice in one day.

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:58.968
You were on the Luck floor
this morning, right?

00:05:58.968 --> 00:06:00.934
-Yes, that was me.

00:06:00.934 --> 00:06:02.834
-I thought so.

00:06:02.834 --> 00:06:08.133
Luck levels
looking excellent as usual.

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:10.634
See you next week.

00:06:10.634 --> 00:06:12.934
Oh, I'm so happy. There are
so few creatures here

00:06:12.934 --> 00:06:16.000
I can actually look in the eye.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.501
We lucky ladies of stature

00:06:17.501 --> 00:06:19.601
ought to stick together,
don't you think?

00:06:19.601 --> 00:06:20.834
-Yeah, come on.

00:06:20.834 --> 00:06:26.934
That's Jane Fonda in "Luck."

00:06:26.934 --> 00:06:28.567
I always love having you here.

00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:30.300
I'm honored that you come
and do our show.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.634
And we always have fun together.

00:06:31.634 --> 00:06:32.701
And I thought tonight --

00:06:32.701 --> 00:06:33.834
We like to play games
on this show.

00:06:33.834 --> 00:06:35.767
And I thought, would you
like to play a game?

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:37.200
And you said yes.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.868
And then I told you
the type of game,

00:06:38.868 --> 00:06:40.834
and you still kind of said yes.
But you haven't said no.

00:06:40.834 --> 00:06:43.133
But now we're live on TV,
so you can't really say no.

00:06:43.133 --> 00:06:44.767
[ Laughter ]
So when we come back,

00:06:44.767 --> 00:06:47.801
we're going to play a game of
"Egg Roulette" with Jane.

